---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About The Kitchen Calc"
  description="Learn about The Kitchen Calc — free, no-sign-up kitchen calculators for American home cooks. Built to help you scale recipes, convert cooking times, and plan holiday meals."
  canonical="https://thekitchencalc.com/about/"
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-secondary mb-6">
      About The Kitchen Calc
    </h1>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-border p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-text-light leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong>The Kitchen Calc</strong> was built for one reason: cooking math
        should be easy. Whether you're doubling grandma's cookie recipe or
        figuring out how much turkey to buy for 20 people, the last thing you
        want to do is pull out a calculator and start doing fractions in your
        head.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        We make free, no-sign-up kitchen calculators that work great on your phone.
        Open the page, punch in your numbers, get your answer — and get back to
        cooking. That's it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">What We Offer</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Recipe Servings Calculator</strong> — Scale any recipe up or down with fraction-friendly results.</li>
        <li><strong>Cooking Time Calculator</strong> — Adjust times for altitude, cooking method, meat doneness, and weight.</li>
        <li><strong>Holiday Meal Planner</strong> — Get a complete shopping list for Thanksgiving, Christmas, or Easter.</li>
        <li><strong>Kitchen Measurement Converter</strong> — Convert cups to grams, tablespoons to milliliters, and more with ingredient-specific density.</li>
        <li><strong>Baking Pan Size Converter</strong> — Adjust recipes between different pan sizes and shapes.</li>
        <li><strong>Oven Temperature Converter</strong> — Convert between Fahrenheit, Celsius, and gas marks.</li>
        <li><strong>Ingredient Substitution Finder</strong> — Find tested substitutes for missing pantry staples.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">How We're Funded</h2>
      <p>
        The Kitchen Calc is supported by advertising. All tools remain free —
        there's no "premium" tier and we don't charge for anything. If you find
        the site helpful, sharing it with a fellow home cook is the best way to
        support us.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">Our Values</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>No sign-ups.</strong> You shouldn't need an account to scale a recipe.</li>
        <li><strong>No data collection.</strong> Everything runs in your browser. We don't store your recipes or meal plans.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile-first.</strong> Built for the kitchen counter, not the office desk.</li>
        <li><strong>US-focused.</strong> We default to the units American home cooks actually use.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        The calculators on this site provide estimates based on standard
        culinary ratios and USDA guidelines. They are for informational and
        entertainment purposes only. Results are not professional cooking,
        nutritional, or medical advice. Always use a food thermometer and follow
        food safety best practices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
